## Import

Import is supported using `project_slug/fingerprint`:

```shell
terraform import circleci_checkout_key.deploy "github/my-org/my-repo/c9:0b:1c:4f:d5:65:56:b9:ad:88:f9:81:2b:37:74:2f"
```

The project slug itself contains slashes, so the import ID is split at the **last** slash: everything before it is the project slug and everything after it is the fingerprint. Use the MD5 fingerprint, which is what the API returns by default and what this resource records; a SHA256 fingerprint contains slashes of its own and cannot be split unambiguously.

## Replacement, not update

The CircleCI API has no endpoint for updating a checkout key, so `project_slug` and `type` both force replacement. Changing either destroys the key and creates a new one with a **new fingerprint** — update any `add_ssh_keys` step, or reference `circleci_checkout_key.<name>.fingerprint` so it follows automatically.

The private half of the key is never returned by the API, so it is never stored in state. Only `public_key` is available.
